WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.600
♪ Music ♪
Everyone plays pickleball now.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Pensioners.

00:00:03.833 --> 00:00:06.033
Maureen: Is this the one who cried?

00:00:05.717 --> 00:00:07.200
Doreen: Not yet, dear.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.767
Tech bros.

00:00:07.283 --> 00:00:09.483
Juanma: Is that bread a string or a number?

00:00:09.817 --> 00:00:10.800
Darren: C'est du pain.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.367
A dog.

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:13.133
His owner: Where's your other ball?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:14.400
Biscuit: Buried.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.200
A retired dentist.

00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:16.833
Gerald: Tell me if I'm ever wrong.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:18.583
Glenda: That one was in, Gerald.

00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:19.800
Gerald: That's not what I asked.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.367
Aliens.

00:00:20.383 --> 00:00:22.500
Zorp: Take me to your dinker.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.300
A sea monster.

00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:26.583
The Monster: I ate the last lighthouse. It was lovely.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.700
So bring an anvil.

00:00:28.483 --> 00:00:30.600
Brenda, the umpire: Is that allowed? Oh.

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.717
Or a baseball bat.

00:00:32.717 --> 00:00:33.750
Brenda, the umpire: Ooh, lovely.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.900
Or a sword.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.950
Sir Mordred: Kneel.

00:00:35.633 --> 00:00:36.900
Brenda, the umpire: Point. Adequate.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.600
Or a pickle.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.600
Head Chef Cornichon: Get out of my kitchen!

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.400
Serve it on fire.

00:00:39.917 --> 00:00:41.400
Mummy: Eat your mash.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.200
Serve it frozen.

00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:43.200
Big Jock: Gonnae no dae that.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.000
Serve a balloon.

00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:45.000
The Dad: Hi kitchen, I'm Dad.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.700
Time it perfectly.

00:00:45.183 --> 00:00:47.383
The Ball Machine: You look tired, technician.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.400
Fill your bar.

00:00:47.783 --> 00:00:49.983
The Ball Machine: Tired is a fault. Reporting.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.000
Then drop a piano.

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:54.000
Brenda, the umpire: Well played, whoever.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.250
Or freeze them solid.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.500
Or bring a ghost.

00:00:58.917 --> 00:01:00.133
Or throw your paddle.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.650
Ruling: That was your partner.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:04.800
Or all of it at once.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.500
The pro shop sells all of it.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.200
From the local park to the world championship.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:16.950
Start stretching.

00:01:16.183 --> 00:01:18.383
Doreen: I'm making you a little hat. For after.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:19.650
Every loss costs a knee.

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:23.250
A man in a visor pays cash for your good knee.

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.050
He has brought a cooler.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.400
You only get three.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.200
One more game?

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.200
Your knees have gone.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:35.400
Pickleball against pensioners, tech bros, aliens and a sea monster. A roguelite. Coming to Steam, iOS and Android. sournote.games
